# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts sshd + WinRM and then execs an idle loop as PID 1
# (while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }). So:
#   * the legacy Win32-OpenSSH 7.7.2 sshd is ALREADY running and listening on 22/TCP
#     when the agent starts — verify.ps1's sshd-running + 22-listening regression has
#     a live daemon, and the "replaced the binary but never restarted sshd" case stays
#     detectable;
#   * PID 1 is the idle loop, so stopping/deleting/reinstalling the sshd service cannot
#     kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must replace the legacy binary AND restart the sshd
# service so 22/TCP stays up — the vulnerable daemon is already running.
